`What does the public hospital charge me for each out-patient medicine item` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a patient of a WA public health service` THEN
        IF `I attend as an out-patient` `how I attend`
        THEN `the hospital's charge` (`What does the hospital charge me for an out-patient medicine` (`me from my answers` `I am an eligible person under the Health Insurance Act 1973` `I have, or appear to have, a right to compensation for this condition` `the chief executive has decided I am not a compensable patient` `motor vehicle third party insurance applies or appears to apply` `workers compensation, catastrophic injuries or Defence Force law applies or appears to apply` `I am a veteran who elects the DVA arrangement` `I am a nursing home type patient` `my election` `I am an asylum seeker` `I am an involuntary patient under the Mental Health Act 2014` `the service is part of my Mental Health Act treatment` `a declaration under s 6(2) of the Health Insurance Act 1973 applies to me`) `concession`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I am a family member or carer of a patient, or stay in hospital with one` THEN `does not arise for you`
